/**
 * The token arena of the front end after the lexer (port of caspien.token.Token; generated by scratch tooling, edit freely).
 * Struct-of-arrays: every Token field is a column indexed by the token's `u64` id, so token links (`left`, `right`, `next`, `chk.catchTry` ...) are plain integers
 * with `TOK_NONE` meaning "none". List-valued fields (`childs`, `sub`, `pinned`, `decorators`, ...) hold a list id into `lists`; two tokens sharing a list id
 * share the list, exactly like the Java aliasing (`gathered.childs = block.childs`), and edits are in place. String-valued fields live in string columns
 * (null = unset); the file name is interned in `files`. See docs/ASTGeneratorPort.md, "Design decisions".
 * An owned `TokStore` is threaded through the parser stages (`ts = ? f(ts, ..)`), because a `ref` to it would die at every allocation (ProofKills).
 */
const TOK_NONE 18446744073709551615

